WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:05.925
This is the last Deck lesson, and it’s about being a professional when something has gone wrong.

2
00:00:06.175 --> 00:00:11.400
As a commercial operator, you must report marine casualties to the Coast Guard.

3
00:00:11.650 --> 00:00:13.300
So what counts?

4
00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:16.925
An unintended grounding, or striking a bridge.

5
00:00:17.175 --> 00:00:22.825
A loss of propulsion, steering or control that reduces your ability to maneuver.

6
00:00:23.075 --> 00:00:27.050
Anything that affects seaworthiness, like a fire or flooding.

7
00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:32.800
A death, or an injury that needs professional medical treatment beyond first aid.

8
00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:39.225
Property damage over seventy-five thousand dollars, or significant harm to the environment.

9
00:00:39.475 --> 00:00:41.150
So try this.

10
00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:46.450
You touch a sandbar on the way in, back off without damage, and nobody’s hurt.

11
00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:48.625
Do you have to report it?

12
00:00:49.625 --> 00:00:51.025
Yes.

13
00:00:51.275 --> 00:00:53.625
It’s an unintended grounding.

14
00:00:53.875 --> 00:00:56.450
The rule doesn’t ask how hard you hit.

15
00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:58.675
When in doubt, report it.
